            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Molly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Interesting flavor to this salad. The next time I make it I'm going to mix the lemon juice, olive oil and sour cream together before adding to the lettuce mixture. My husband doesn't care for sour cream and wondered what the \"white stuff\" was. I told him it was yogurt! I think mixing the 3 ingredients together first will help tame the sour cream. I really enjoyed this. Thanks Gianna for sharing."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sharon B"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I cut the salt completely, and allowed guests to \"salt-to-taste\". I also Put the dressing in a bowl, so the guests could spoon over the dressing. Which eliminates lettuce wilting. Everyone loved the salad:-)\nA bit too much parsley for my taste. Next time I will half the parsley:-). I will definitely make this salad again! Thanks for sharing Gianna!",
            "datePublished": "2019-11-04T16:24:28.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "stacey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was super easy to make and everyone loved the flavor of the dressing. I mixed the sour cream with the lemon juice and olive oil and chilled it until ready to serve. I then tossed it with the salad immediately before serving and it created a very smooth dressing. I was concerned it would be too \"lemony\" tasting but once it mixed in with all the salad ingredients it was just right.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-19T03:43:45.793Z"
          },
          {
